s>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhao</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Knapp</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>James</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name><article-title>Crystal structure of human beta-hexosaminidase B: understanding the molecular basis of Sandhoff and Tay-Sachs disease</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><year>2003</year><volume>327</volume><fpage>1093</fpage><lpage>1109</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0022-2836(03)00216-X</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12662933</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Lemieux</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mark</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Cherney</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Withers</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Mahuran</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>James</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name><article-title>Crystallographic structure of human beta-hexosaminidase A: interpretation of Tay-Sachs mutations and loss of GM2 ganglioside hydrolysis</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><year>2006</year><volume>359</volume><fpage>913</fpage><lpage>929</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jmb.2006.04.004</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16698036</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Korneluk</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Mahuran</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Neote</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Klavins</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Dowd</surname><given-names>BF</given-names></name><name><surname>Tropak</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Willard</surname><given-names>HF</given-names></name><name><surname>Ander